        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6cbacd1d-54fd-55d7-a172-3ecd164fb66f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Lantana, Silybum, milk thistle\n- Animals: Strymon bazochii\n- Taxonomy: Verbenaceae, daisy family\n- Places: Hawaii\n- Topics: biological control, plant genera\n\nFacts:\n- Lantana is a genus of about 150 species of perennial flowering plants in the verbena family, Verbenaceae.\n- Silybum, also called milk thistle, is a genus of two species of thistles in the daisy family.\n- In 1902, Strymon bazochii was introduced to Hawaii to control Lantana species.\n- Strymon bazochii proved unsuccessful at controlling Lantana species in Hawaii.",
